  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>

  <header>
    <div class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cat FAQ</p>
      <h1>Everything you wanted to know about cats</h1>
      <p>Quick answers about cat behavior, care, and what makes these curious companions so lovable.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content">
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-answer-1">
          <span class="question">Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="cat-answer-1" hidden>
          <p>Cats often knead when they feel relaxed and safe. The motion comes from kittenhood, when kneading helped stimulate milk flow. Adult cats may keep the habit as a comfort behavior or to mark a favorite spot with scent glands in their paws.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-answer-2">
          <span class="question">Why do cats purr?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="cat-answer-2" hidden>
          <p>Purring can mean a cat is content, but it can also appear when a cat is nervous, hurt, or seeking comfort. It's one of the ways cats communicate emotional state, and the vibration often has a soothing effect for both cat and human.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-answer-3">
          <span class="question">How much sleep do cats need?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="cat-answer-3" hidden>
          <p>Most cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day, with kittens and senior cats often sleeping even more. Their sleep patterns are naturally built around short bursts of energy, so naps help them stay ready for play, hunting instincts, and exploring.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cat-answer-4">
          <span class="question">Why do cats bring home toys or prey?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="cat-answer-4" hidden>
          <p>This behavior can be a mix of instinct, play, and social sharing. In a household, a cat may treat people like part of the family and bring back a "gift" or practice hunting skills through toys, socks, and other movable objects.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer>
    Built for quick browsing, with each answer hidden until you choose to expand it.
  </footer>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.example').forEach((item) => {
      const button = item.querySelector('.toggle');
      const panel = item.querySelector('.details');

      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const expanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
        item.classList.toggle('is-open', !expanded);
        panel.hidden = expanded;
      });
    });
  </script>
